  "result": "The gate passed on `NRS_484B_410_o1`: it returned **OK** (10 witnesses, 14 names, composes nothing).\n\n**How the rule is written** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_410_o1.lean`):\n- **Class:** the subject is a member of the vehicle aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When the rule applies (the start):** the subject is not halted now, but at the previous observation it was halted, on a highway, and not in a no-parking place. In Lean this is `¬halt ∧ rises(¬(halt ∧ onHighway ∧ ¬noParkingPlace))`, so the highway and the exception are both read at the previous observation, as the node says.\n- **No-parking place (the exception):** either a curb zone the subject occupies whose kind is no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane, or whose curb is painted red; or a travel region the subject occupies that a no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping sign governs, with the sign's conditions holding.\n- **Obligation:** no other road user is predicted to come within the conflict clearance of the subject within the conflict horizon. A road user predicted to come that close is a violation.\n- I added no narrowings: the formulas state exactly what the node's applicability says.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_410_o1.lean`):\n- The five planned scenes pass: forbid, permit, idle, blind and branch_1.\n- I added five more so that every part of the formulas changes some verdict:\n  - **branch_2:** a red curb alone, without a no-parking kind (not applicable).\n  - **branch_3:** a no-parking curb kind alone, unpainted (not applicable).\n  - **branch_4:** an unconditional no-parking sign (not applicable).\n  - **branch_5:** a weekday-only sign on a Sunday, so the duty applies (violated).\n  - **branch_6:** a car passing 5 m away in the next lane (compliant).\n- Every witness judges only the observations at 1 s and 2 s. At the first observation there is no earlier one to compare against, so the start would read as unknown there.\n\n**Process slips:**\n- I used 2 of the 6 gate runs. The first was an unnecessary baseline on the untouched skeleton; it returned UNUSED_CLAIM because the formulas were still empty.\n- I also ran one shell command that was not the gate (a no-op `true`), against the one-command rule.\n\nBoth slips and the choices above are recorded in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
